  <prompt>Implement the H14 post-deploy integration wiring handler as an IJobHandler in the L2 control plane per spec.md FR-19. H14 has 3 DAG-parallel sub-handlers: (a) 2 Exchange ApplicationAccessPolicy — one for BFF app-reg + one for UAMI, T4 action-and-verify semantics (on 0 or 1 → create; on 2+ → verify AppIds match else fail with drift diagnostic); (b) Graph webhook subscriptions per Communication/Email module with HMAC signing keys from H4 (task 047); (c) Dataverse service-endpoint webhooks. S2S consent sub-step (d) explicitly NOT included (r3 task 060 dropped). Idempotency key: h14-{customerId}-{subStep}-{hash}.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in IJobHandler contract (ADR-004), Exchange Set-ApplicationAccessPolicy PowerShell semantics, Graph webhook subscription lifecycle (Microsoft.Graph v6), Dataverse service-endpoint plugin webhooks, and HMAC signing keys from KV. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>File src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H14IntegrationWiringHandler.cs exists, implements IJobHandler, decomposes into 3 DAG-parallel sub-handlers (H14a Exchange, H14b Graph webhooks, H14c Dataverse webhooks), registers in L2 DI, and each sub-handler asserts idempotency + reports outcome. T4 action-and-verify semantics enforced by H14a. Unit tests cover happy paths + T4 drift-diagnostic path.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-19 + T4 + design.md §4.1 H14 row + §4B trap catalog: H14 is the LAST handler before H13 acceptance. Its 3 sub-handlers wire the customer environment into external systems (Exchange for mailflow, Graph for change notifications, Dataverse plugins for webhooks). T4 is the silent-fail trap where policy count == 2+ but principals don't match — H14a explicitly detects this drift. r3 task 060 dropped S2S — so no (d) sub-step; do NOT re-introduce.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H14IntegrationWiringHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H14aExchangePolicySubHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H14bGraphWebhookSubHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H14cDataverseWebhookSubHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H14IntegrationWiringHandler.Tests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/IdempotencyService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="047" status="pending">H4 KV secrets population — provides HMAC signing keys consumed by H14b</dependency>
      <dependency task="053" status="pending">H10 Dataverse App User + Graph app-role parity — H14 assumes UAMI has Exchange.ManageAsApp role</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-19">SCOPE: 3 sub-handlers only — Exchange policies + Graph webhooks + Dataverse service-endpoint webhooks; S2S consent (d) explicitly NOT included per r3 task 060.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md T4">SCOPE: Exchange policy count semantics: 0 or 1 → create missing; 2+ → verify BOTH principals match BFF-app-reg + UAMI; if not, fail with drift diagnostic. No silent overwrite.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">SCOPE: H14 is one IJobHandler that spawns 3 sub-handlers via internal DAG-parallel dispatch; each sub-handler has its own idempotency key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">SCOPE: Registers in L2 control-plane DI container, NOT the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">SCOPE: 3-level idempotency per sub-handler (MessageId + Redis lock + deterministic key h14-{customerId}-{subStep}-{hash}).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4D I5">SCOPE: Graph SDK calls in H14b pass explicit tenantId; Exchange PS invocations use per-tenant scoped credentials.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: HMAC signing keys for Graph webhooks come from H4-populated KV secrets (task 047); do NOT generate ad-hoc keys in H14.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: NFR-09 — Graph SDK v6 / Kiota 2.0 — catch ODataError (not ServiceException).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§6.5">SCOPE: R22 Exchange RBAC-for-Applications migration is Phase D backlog for r2 (NOT r1) — H14a uses current Set-ApplicationAccessPolicy pattern; coexistence safe per Q5 spike.</constraint>
  </constraints>

