  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load spec.md FR-19 + T4 + design.md §4.1 H14 row.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Author main">Author H14IntegrationWiringHandler.cs as the parent; dispatches 3 sub-handlers in parallel via internal DAG.</step>
    <step order="2" name="H14a Exchange">Author H14aExchangePolicySubHandler.cs — Get-ApplicationAccessPolicy; 0/1 → New-ApplicationAccessPolicy for missing; 2+ → verify AppIds match; else fail with drift diagnostic (T4 semantics).</step>
    <step order="3" name="H14b Graph webhooks">Author H14bGraphWebhookSubHandler.cs — read HMAC signing keys from KV (H4 provisioned per task 047); create/update Graph subscriptions per Communication/Email module. Use Graph v6 with explicit tenantId (I5); catch ODataError.</step>
    <step order="4" name="H14c Dataverse webhooks">Author H14cDataverseWebhookSubHandler.cs — register Dataverse service-endpoint webhook records with signing keys.</step>
    <step order="5" name="No S2S">Explicit code assertion: no S2S consent sub-step present; startup verification.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Register">Register all 4 handlers (main + 3 sub) in L2 Program.cs DI.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Tests">Unit tests: H14a T4 drift path (2 policies, mismatched principals → fail with drift diagnostic); H14a happy (0 → creates 2); H14b happy; H14c happy; idempotency per sub-handler.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Verify">dotnet build + dotnet test = green; dotnet format; zero analyzer warnings.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 073 → ✅.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbors: 13 production IJobHandlers under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/**. Grep for `IntegrationWiring` or `Exchange*Handler` returns none. No existing post-deploy integration handler.</existing>
    <extension>No — H14 orchestrates 3 distinct external-system integrations (Exchange PS, Graph webhooks, Dataverse webhooks) that each have their own auth ceremony + T4-style drift semantics. Extending a single-integration handler would violate ADR-004's "one message one handler one outcome" for sub-integrations.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without H14, the customer environment reaches Setup Status = Ready but Exchange mailflow, Graph change notifications, and Dataverse webhooks are all unconfigured. Communication/Email module fails silently at first user interaction; T4 policy drift persists (spec.md §4B T4 explicitly cites this failure mode). H14 IS the last-mile integration handler.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

